# kk,wsi/metal: Support additional HDR formats / color spaces
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46803 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

The existing logic in KosmicKrisp only supports a subset of potential HDR texture formats / color spaces, excluding common combinations such as `VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32` / `VK_COLOR_SPACE_HDR10_ST2084_EXT`. This change adds support for additional combinations.

The specific set of texture formats / color spaces that Apple supports EDR with is unfortunately not well documented. There is a diagram shown in a WWDC 2022 presentation (https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2022/10113/?time=755), though it is not an exhaustive list. I manually tested combinations of texture formats and color spaces to determine which are supported for EDR.

With this change, the behavior of HDR rendering matches MoltenVK, with the exception that MoltenVK does not support HDR for `VK_COLOR_SPACE_ADOBERGB_NONLINEAR_EXT`.
